# Redirect non-trailing-slash to trailing-slash (canonical) for all known paths
# This ensures consistent URLs matching sitemap and canonical tags
# Root (/) does not need a trailing slash redirect
# SPECIFIC PATHS FIRST (before wildcards) to avoid redirect chains
https://numbersystemconverter.com/about https://numbersystemconverter.com/about/ 301!
https://numbersystemconverter.com/contact https://numbersystemconverter.com/contact/ 301!
https://numbersystemconverter.com/privacy-policy https://numbersystemconverter.com/privacy-policy/ 301!
https://numbersystemconverter.com/terms https://numbersystemconverter.com/terms/ 301!

# Also handle www versions of non-trailing-slash paths (specific before wildcard)
www.numbersystemconverter.com/about https://numbersystemconverter.com/about/ 301!
www.numbersystemconverter.com/contact https://numbersystemconverter.com/contact/ 301!
www.numbersystemconverter.com/privacy-policy https://numbersystemconverter.com/privacy-policy/ 301!
www.numbersystemconverter.com/terms https://numbersystemconverter.com/terms/ 301!

# Redirect www to non-www (HTTPS) - using domain pattern
www.numbersystemconverter.com/* https://numbersystemconverter.com/:splat 301!

# Redirect HTTP to HTTPS non-www
http://numbersystemconverter.com/* https://numbersystemconverter.com/:splat 301!
http://www.numbersystemconverter.com/* https://numbersystemconverter.com/:splat 301!